# Console shutdown regression — the EOF path (CTRL-D at the prompt).
#
#   bin/metatron-docker build console --steps bin/test/console-eof.steps
#
# ctrl-D at an empty prompt raises EndOfFileException in the console's read
# loop.  The fix routes it through the same close-and-drain sequence as :quit —
# the render queue is drained and the terminal is handed back before the process
# goes — and the process exits.  (The drain/close itself is proven end-to-end by
# console-quit.steps and by FloatingSurfaceTest.shouldNotReturnUntilEnqueuedRenderTasksHaveRun;
# ctrl-D calls the very same Console.close().)
#
# What THIS scenario can and does assert: ctrl-D ends the process — so the pty
# closes and the harness reports "the vm exited early" — instead of hanging.
# (The harness stops stepping once the pty is closed, so post-exit text cannot
# be asserted here; a hang leaves no "vm exited early" marker and leaves the VM
# alive, which is how a regression would show up.)

WAIT_CONSOLE

# --- the console is live before we end it ---
MARK live
SEND 1
WAIT ==>1

# --- ctrl-D at the prompt ends the console; the pump below is what lets the
#     harness observe the pty close and report "the vm exited early" ---
MARK eof
KEY ctrl+d
SLEEP 1
